# Continuous Scoring Tasks

- Use this style for dataset tasks where score is a continuous function of submitted predictions, not a rubric. See `docs/ML_TASKS.md`.
- Set `[difficulty].task_type = "ml"` and `[difficulty].reward_type = "continuous_scoring_function"` (this template's enum has no `dataset` type; the submission shape is expressed via the loader you call, not the task_type).
- `ml` tasks must declare `[difficulty].license`: a permissive SPDX id from `task_metadata.LICENSES`, or `self_generated` for fully synthetic data.
- Read agent artifacts only via sanctioned component-safe loaders (for example
  `helpers.load_submission_or_fault(...)`; use
  `helpers.open_submission_file_or_fault(...)` for a custom file-like parser).
  Never hand-roll `lstat` or leaf-only `O_NOFOLLOW`. Read hidden targets from
  `private`. Prefer sealed `ContinuousTask.model()` / `TASK.grade(...)` over
  legacy hand curves.
- **Committed-strategy contract (mandatory):** every reference/naive declares digest-bound artifacts and an inference-only entrypoint. Existing trained models may keep `model.manifest.json`; use `strategy.manifest.json` with explicit `trained_model` or `committed_artifact` kind for procedural training and hand-authored policies/static artifacts. Never invent training data. Trusted CI / ground-truth / seal never train.
- Numeric tabular tasks retain built-in no-information probes. Non-tabular callbacks declare deterministic ready-to-measure workspaces under `baselines/degenerate/` with `WorkspaceDegenerateProbes`; any missing/faulting/nondeterministic probe fails calibration.
- Reference must score `0.5 ± 0.05`; naive is weak-positive by default. A naive that exactly ties every effective no-information floor needs `naive_score_min=0` plus a reviewed `naive_at_floor` rationale.
- Sized private challenges use `selection_policy="stable_subset"` (now the
  default); `artifact_digest` is legacy-lock migration only. Static CSVs with
  IDs declare `join_key`.
- New classification-heavy tasks should set
  `GeneratedCalibration(quality_floor_mode="effective_no_info")` so prevalence
  below the no-information ceiling earns no grade-time credit.
- Prompts must disclose every `PythonPredictor` load/predict, row, and serialized
  reply limit committed in the task spec.
- Do not introduce `RubricTask` / rubric criteria unless the task is actually decomposed into deterministic rubric checks (`reward_type = "multi_deterministic_rubrics"`).
- Before opening or updating a PR, run `uv run lbx-rl-harness run --runtime ground-truth --problem-dir problems/<task_id>` (inference-only; never shells out to `train.py`). While iterating, use `uv run lbx-rl-harness reference --problem-dir problems/<task_id>`.
